<title>USA: Rhone-Poulenc says board okays repurchase.</title>
<headline>Rhone-Poulenc says board okays repurchase.</headline>
<dateline>COLLEGEVILLE, Pa. 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rhone-Poulenc Rorer said Thursday its directors had approved a plan to buy back up to five million of its shares to finance employee benefits.</p>
<p>&quot;The repurchased shares will be held by a flexible employee benefits trust to finance certain existing U.S. employee benefits, including savings plan, stock plan and pension programs,&quot; the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>The repurchase program will begin immediately on the open market, the company added.</p>
</text>
